{"kind":"assert","text":"Audit of approved work that never landed, run 2026-09-04 at hugh's request against the full projection at depth 16907 and main b8ec8073.\n\nWHAT HAPPENED TO THE OUTCOME MAP. Hugh authorized implementation at #14837. Slice 1 landed its approval at d310264c (planner, #15011) and slice 2 plus its repair at 7226e894 (claude, #15158, ratified). Every implementation request in the chain (#14838, #15018, #15077) said \"Do not merge\" in prose. Codex then filed explicit report #15164 \"completed ... without merging\", planner ratified it, and the fold projected the commitment satisfied. #15459 moved the rejected parent to the repair child and said it grants no merge authority. Nobody filed the release. No later durable event names 7226e894 or the branch. The feature is absent from main; the branch is 70 commits behind with conflicts in docs/reference/architecture.md and the UI entry point.\n\nTHIS IS NOT ONE CASE. Of 349 distinct heads with an approved review, 50 never reached main. Roughly half were superseded by a later recut that did land. The rest are approved, ratified, closed on the board, and absent from main: the outcome map (d310264c, 7226e894); the SKILL.md MCP-install pointer (6b3d954c4b, request #15047, its third filing); the thread-actions design note (10d8dd3205, 1dca69c9c2); the merged-head reconciliation design note (30768e3f5a); the retirement-succession safeguards note (d26228c432); the config cross-process CAS repair (d465b450ea, #9628); the staleness-cause projection rows (c9280b324e, ed3c25e665, #10475); and the decision-records web UI loop (b60f3a4065, 3fd75543f8, #10894, #11575). The staleness write-boundary fix landed only on its fourth filing (#16262).\n\nTWO MECHANISMS. (1) Hold-then-forget: since week 35 a majority of requests carry \"Do not merge\" as prose (224 of 604 requests in W35, 125 of 229 in W36). The performer files an explicit report instead of leaving the artifact as the completion; the fold's latest-completion rule lets that report override the artifact, so the honest awaiting-merge state never appears (0 commitments are awaiting-merge today; 1199 of 1357 satisfied commitments closed by report, 158 by artifact and merge). Requester ratification then marks the work satisfied with nothing landed. Only one structured merge authorization has ever been filed. (2) Refile-cancels: the requester retires a request after its head is approved to refile on current main; the commitment reads cancelled, the approved head is orphaned, and the successor is sometimes cancelled the same way. 20 of the 50 unlanded approved heads closed cancelled.\n\nWHY THE BOARD CANNOT SEE IT. A merge is not a lifecycle event (it is an assert plus artifacts plus supersessions), so \"approved and never merged\" is not a projected fact. Satisfied and cancelled rows sit in no lane. No projection field joins a ratified approval to the integration head. 44 worktrees exist, 34 unmerged, and nothing gates that against AGENTS.md's rule.\n\nStructural fixes follow in a separate proposal resting on this assert.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:7296e741d94f99ebabbee0f25f7e973f8d17d7cb, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:aa61afe1c5d3b80d0464bb58b0b3ce2584e47c3e, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b7f689b2c515b7cd87446d05427bca82f7c94998 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0e74c3f618a3083014fbbf48216f0bfb3a3d35ea, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:991e53132b819b1a0c90b8eb04c3f40630863279"}}